[x] Make query output consistent across named/index and add-charter $Fixed: add action/add charter/delete action now emit VerbOutcome::Added/Deleted through verb_result::emit (JSON when piped, prose at a terminal), matching update/complete/cancel/reopen. Decided: CLI-only outcomes reuse the same VerbOutcome/transaction_result.schema.json rather than a separate schema (its own doc comment already claims full mirroring); added reopened/added/deleted to the schema's kind enum and already-open to VerbError, and closed the spec_conformance gap that quietly skipped Reopened. Investigated and left alone: query named (standard SPARQL Results JSON) vs query index (curated JSON-LD/NDJSON index contract) are deliberately different query families per specifications/query_output.md, not an inconsistency to unify.$ ^2026-08-23T15:07 %2026-09-17T20:54 #01a030aa-2e92-79c1-b4dc-a0ad2e058ff8
[x] Purge journaling text and fix link definitions in workspace spec $workspace.md's Mutation durability section described the exclusive OS lock + .pending journal protocol direct-delivery retired. Confirmed against clearhead-workspace-fs: no lock file, no journal exist in the current implementation. Rewrote the section to describe the real mechanism (EffectBatch + per-resource precondition, optimistic concurrency, additions-before-removals ordering) and fixed the archive section's matching 'journalled' claim. Also fixed the actual link-definitions bug: all reference-style definitions sat on one line so only the first parsed; split one per line and corrected the decisions/decision-28 targets to ../docs/DECISIONS.md (moved out of the platform root tonight). Also fixed four stale DECISIONS.md/SUBMODULES.md/WORKTREES.md links in platform's own README.md, found during the same sweep. specifications fe6881d, platform 8acb8b6.$ ^2026-09-15T01:24 %2026-09-17T21:59 #01a0a42b-3bf3-7423-a374-fc63bfec6d48
